Reserved in any block: `auto` (UI-only, not passed to tools).

## Orchestrator delegation

```bash
node .ai/runtime/orchestrator-state.mjs active-runtime
node .ai/runtime/orchestrator-state.mjs model-hint --role review --review-depth <simple|full>
```

- **Do not** pass `--runtime cursor` when you are in Codex (or the reverse).
- `--review-depth full` promotes the review to the `quality` tier even when the configured default role tier is `budget`; `simple` keeps the configured tier.
- Override detection: `AIFORGE_ACTIVE_RUNTIME=codex` (or `cursor`, `claude`).
- Follow JSON `instruction` and pass the preference only to the active host's native subagent tool. If explicit model selection is unavailable, inherit a compatible native model and record the fallback.
- Never turn a model hint into a shell-launched agent CLI or PTY polling loop.

## Editing

Change tiers in `agents.modelTiers`. Add slugs under `agents.runtimeModels.<runtime>.<tier>`. Re-run `sync` to refresh `.ai/project.model-profiles.json`.

`saveConfig` / `loadConfig` rejects obvious cross-runtime slug mistakes (e.g. `gpt-5.5-medium` under `codex`).
